  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>.</mo></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> be the set of points in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> at which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is not differentiable. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>",
