  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given function is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\" separators=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>The graph of the function, is</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0586fe52-962a-400c-b729-b64749754feb-139.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 210px;\" /></p><p>We know that, a function is not differentiable at a point where its graph has a sharp corner.</p><p>And, from the graph we can easily conclude that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is non-derivable at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the set&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
